          <h2 class="section-title">OT/IT convergence creates new operational risk</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Power generation, water treatment and oil and gas facilities rely on SCADA systems that were traditionally air-gapped. As operators integrate these systems with enterprise IT for real-time analytics and remote management, the attack surface expands significantly.</p>
          <p>Protecting operational technology requires specialised approaches — protocol-aware monitoring, industrial network segmentation and zero-trust access controls. Standard IT security tools are often inadequate for the unique protocols and availability requirements of industrial control systems.</p>
